        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): classify commandExecution mutability via shared isMutatingToolCall",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #101890 — strict-agentic retry cannot retry terminal turns that only\nperformed read-only inspection tools because `isMutatingNativeToolItem` always\ntreats `commandExecution` items as mutating.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`isMutatingNativeToolItem` returns `true` for all `commandExecution` items,\nclassifying even read-only commands (grep, ls, rg, cat) as having side effects.\nThis prevents strict-agentic retry from re-running terminal turns that only\ninspected the workspace.\n\n## Fix\n\n1. Export `isMutatingToolCall` through the plugin SDK (`agent-harness-runtime`)\n   alongside the already-exported `isReplaySafeToolCall`\n2. Use `isMutatingToolCall(\"exec\", itemToolArgs(item))` in\n   `isMutatingNativeToolItem` instead of the blanket `return true`\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Source-Level Proof\n\n`isMutatingToolCall` correctly classifies read-only shell commands via the\nshared `READ_ONLY_SHELL_COMMANDS` allowlist (cat, grep, head, ls, pwd, rg,\nstat, tail, wc):\n\n```\nisMutatingToolCall(\"exec\", { command: \"rg TODO src\" })   → false (read-only)\nisMutatingToolCall(\"exec\", { command: \"grep foo .\" })    → false (read-only)\nisMutatingToolCall(\"exec\", { command: \"cat file.txt\" })  → false (read-only)\nisMutatingToolCall(\"exec\", { command: \"rm -rf /tmp\" })   → true  (mutating)\nisMutatingToolCall(\"exec\", { command: \"echo > /tmp/x\" }) → true  (redirect)\n```\n\n### Regression Test\n\n`outcome-fallback-runtime-contract.test.ts` — 7 table-driven cases verified\nvia the full Codex event projector: read-only commands (rg, grep, ls, cat) →\n`replaySafe: true`; mutating commands (echo redirect, rm, npm install) →\n`replaySafe: false`.\n\n### Call chain verified\n\n```\nisMutatingNativeToolItem → isSideEffectingNativeToolItem → recordToolMeta\n  → sideEffectingToolItemIds → hadPotentialSideEffects → replayMetadata\n```\n\n### Autoreview (claude-sonnet-5)\n\n```\n→ patch is correct (0.98), no accepted/actionable findings\n```\n\n- [x] `oxfmt --check` passes\n- [x] `oxlint` passes\n- [x] SDK surface budget updated\n- [x] autoreview clean (claude-sonnet-5, 0.98)",
